{"type": "thinking", "text": "More options: Clear completed, Collapse subtasks, Expand subtasks, Share. No direction.\n\nHmm. Let's think again about \"global direction setting\". Maybe \"Direction\" refers to \"sort direction\" of Grouping row? In Tasks.org the group/sort dialog = \"Sort\" dialog. The row \"Grouping: By due date Ascending\" and \"Sorting: By title Descending\". Hmm.\n\nActually — Wait. In the Settings > \"Task list options\" there was \"Per-list sorting\" off. If per-list sorting were ON, each list remembers sort/group settings independently. The changed build says \"Sort sheet: the sheet's options are now resolved from the current list's preferences.\" Maybe the bug is in the interaction between \"Subtasks: My order\" and direction? Hmm.\n\nLet me consider possible seeded bugs:\n1. Sort sheet bug: The sort sheet may show the *default* preferences instead of the current list's (e.g., before I changed, it showed \"By due date Ascending\" which matched). With per-list sorting off, all lists share. Hmm, but we could turn on per-list sorting on Default list and My Tasks? Hmm.\n\n2. Subtask nesting bug: In manual mode nested items follow global direction — maybe direction wrong (e.g., when sorting descending, subtasks display ascending) or app crashes.\n\n3. Repeat picker bug: custom recurrence loads wrong rule (e.g., Pay rent shows 1 month/day 4 correct; Water plants showed 1 hour correct; Weekly review showed 2 weeks but days unselected; Final dose showed after 1 occurrence correct). Wait — maybe Weekly review's \"Repeats on\" not selected is indeed the seeded bug? Hmm, but the rule loaded 2 weeks.\n\nLet's test more precisely: For Weekly review, if existing rule is FREQ=WEEKLY;INTERVAL=2;BYDAY=MO, then dialog should show M selected. Since due date is Monday, expected M highlighted. Entry point is \"Custom...\" from picker. Note that when you choose the weekly preset \"Every week\", the custom dialog would probably prefill days. But opening custom shows no days — that might be intentional for a rule with no BYDAY.\n\nHmm, how can I detect? I could check what the rule is by looking at the task's repeat row: \"Repeats every 2 weeks\" — no day info. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: The preconditions say \"Weekly review (due in 30 days, repeats every 2 weeks)\". This is deliberately not saying \"on Mondays\". So the rule likely has no BYDAY. So no day selected is correct.\n\nOK so maybe the repeat picker change is fine. But wait — Pay rent custom showed \"Monthly on day 4\" — that's loaded from rule (BYMONTHDAY=4). Good. Water plants 1 hour. Final dose after 1. All fine.\n\nHmm, so where's the bug? Maybe none in repeat picker. But let's dig into the \"Subtasks in manual mode follow global direction\" more.\n\nMaybe \"global direction setting\" is the Settings > \"Task list options\" > ... hmm no. Or in \"Date and time\"? no.\n\nLet me search: Tasks.org has list \"Sort\" options in a dialog with tabs: \"Group by\", \"Sort by\", \"Subtasks\", \"Manual\" etc. In older versions, there were two separate dialogs: \"Sort\" and \"Group\". Hmm. In this version, the sheet has Grouping, Sorting, Subtasks. The \"Subtasks\" row with \"My order\" — \"manual mode\". The \"global direction setting\" may be the direction toggle on the Sorting row? No...\n\nActually maybe the \"global direction setting\" is Android's \"Force RTL layout direction\" developer option? \"nested items in manual mode now follow the global direction setting\" — if the layout direction is RTL, nested items' indentation direction should flip (indent from right). Hmm! That actually makes sense for \"direction\": the subtask indent/arrow direction follows the layout direction. But \"global direction setting\" in the app? Hmm.\n\nAnother idea: In Tasks.org, tasks have \"manual order\" and the sort dialog has for \"Manual\" mode a sub-option \"Reverse order\" / direction? Let me check the Sorting options list again: By due date, By start date, By priority, By title, By last modified, Smart sort, Created, My order (disabled for My Tasks). So \"My order\" is not selectable for My Tasks. Maybe in Default list, \"My order\" is selectable, and when selected, the direction toggle appears? To test manual mode on the list level, I'd need tasks in Default list — they are! Buy milk's list is Default list, yet Default list view showed empty. That's suspicious.\n\nHold on. Maybe the reason Default list is empty: In the nav drawer, \"Default list\" is under \"Local lists\". But maybe there's a bug: tasks assigned to Default list are not shown because... hmm, but My Tasks shows them. Actually maybe My Tasks is \"all_inbox\" which includes tasks from all lists. If Default list view is empty, that's a genuine bug: tasks in Default list not visible. But wait, maybe the Default list view is filtered by a tag or something? No.\n\nLet me reproduce: open nav drawer, tap Default list, wait, observe. Earlier it showed \"There are no tasks here.\" Let me retry now, maybe it was a transient state right after app open."}
