ttom for new subtasks) follows \"New tasks on top\". Hmm, plausible but weak.\n\nWait, maybe there IS a global \"sort direction\" setting for manual sort in the sort sheet's Sorting options - like \"My order\" has a direction arrow. On Default list, after selecting My order, the sheet showed \"Grouping: None\" (grouping got disabled) and \"Sorting: My order\" (no direction). Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the Grouping options in the sheet: tap Grouping → options list, maybe includes \"None\", \"By due date\", \"By start date\", \"By priority\", \"By tag\", \"By list\"? Not direction.\n\nMaybe direction setting is in Settings > \"Task list options\" but hidden below the visible list? We saw all options ending with Tags at bottom, screen scroll ended? There might be more below: \"Start date\", \"Places\", \"Lists\", \"Tags\" — chips rows. Maybe further down there are \"Completed tasks\" etc. Let me scroll further in Task list options.\n\nActually, the sort sheet has \"Completed | By completion time | Descending\" — this is the sort for completed tasks.\n\nHmm, \"global direction setting\" - could be the \"Sort direction\" of the *subtask sorting* in the sort sheet. Wait, in Tasks.org source there's `SORT_DIRECTION` pref maybe. Let me search my memory of Tasks.org: There's a setting \"Sort direction\" in \"Task list options\"? I believe there is a preference `sort_direction` used for... Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe \"global direction setting\" is in Date and time? no.\n\nLet me examine the sort sheet more. In the sheet, \"Subtasks | My order\" row — tap it shows modes. Maybe there's also an \"Ascending/Descending\" control for the Subtasks row when a non-manual mode is chosen. But the change says manual mode follows the global direction setting, which might mean: when Subtasks = My order, and the global Sorting has Descending direction, the nested manual subtasks should be reversed. Since Sorting by title Descending, maybe subtasks manual order should be reversed too? But manual mode should be about manual order, not title. Hmm.\n\nActually re-read: \"Subtask nesting in the task list: nested items in manual mode now follow the global direction setting.\" I think \"nested items\" = the subtasks. In manual mode (Subtasks: My order), the order of the nested items follows the \"global direction setting\". The global direction setting might be the *sort direction* (ascending/descending) of the list's sort (e.g., \"By title Descending\")? That sounds odd.\n\nOR: \"global direction setting\" might be a global setting \"Manual sort direction\" in Settings > Task defaults? Hmm. \"New tasks on top\" might be exactly the \"global direction setting\" — when unchecked, new tasks go to bottom. For subtasks in manual mode, the directions might be: new subtasks added on top vs bottom according to \"New tasks on top\".\n\nHmm, hmm. Let me look for a \"direction\" setting by searching the Settings screens more thoroughly, including \"Task list options\" scrolled to the bottom, \"Edit screen options\", \"Date and time\". Let me check \"Task list options\" bottom."}
