{"type": "thinking", "text": "Subtasks still Print tickets then Charge phone. So sorting direction does NOT flip subtask manual order. So \"global direction setting\" isn't that, or no change (maybe the seeded bug: it *should* flip but doesn't?).\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe \"the global direction setting\" is a global setting for *manual sort direction* that exists in **Settings > Task defaults > New tasks on top**? That's about where new tasks go. Maybe for subtask nesting: when adding a new subtask, it goes on top if \"New tasks on top\" is checked. That's not \"nested items follow direction\".\n\nAlternatively maybe there's a global setting specifically for **sort direction of manual order** accessible via the sort sheet when \"My order\" is selected — perhaps a \"Sort direction\" row that's missing in this build. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the list's preferences via the \"list settings\" (long-press list in drawer). In Tasks.org, long-pressing a list in nav opens list edit with options maybe including \"Sort direction\". Let me try long-press on Default list in the drawer. It might offer rename/delete. Or the three-dot? Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe \"global direction setting\" = the *sort direction* selected for **Grouping** row. Since grouping \"By due date Ascending\", group headers ascend. Nested items (subtasks) in manual mode now follow \"the global direction setting\" — meaning depending on Ascending/Descending of the list sort, manual subtasks are ordered ascending or descending. But we tested Sorting direction; let's also test Grouping direction. Change Grouping direction to Descending while Sorting is Descending (all directions descending) and see if subtask order flips. Hmm, that's the same expectation.\n\nWait — maybe with Sorting = \"My order\" (manual) selected on a list that supports it, there IS a direction toggle or the direction comes from global. For My Tasks, My order is disabled. So the \"manual mode\" likely means when the *list sort* is My order. On My Tasks we can't select it, but the Subtasks=My order is also \"manual mode\" for nested items. So which one does the change refer to? \"Subtask nesting in the task list: nested items in manual mode now follow the global direction setting.\"\n\nMaybe \"nested items in manual mode\" = in the *task list*, subtasks with \"Subtasks: My order\" — yes.\n\nAnd the \"global direction setting\" might be... Let me look at the app's settings for a \"direction\" more thoroughly. Search in settings screens: \"Edit screen options\", \"Date and time\". Let me quickly scan both. Also \"Notifications\" maybe not.\n\nActually, maybe there's a separate setting under \"Look and feel\" → \"Language\" etc. No.\n\nLet me check \"Edit screen options\"."}
