{"type": "thinking", "text": "Long-press just navigated (no menu). Hmm.\n\nOK, let me think about this differently. The changed statement might be interpreted as: \"nested items in manual mode now follow the global direction setting\" meaning **the order of nested (subtask) rows when the parent is shown in the list in manual sort mode**. There might be a *global direction setting* that is the \"Sort direction\" of the \"Grouping\" — no.\n\nMaybe I should look at the source of Tasks.org (knowledge): In Tasks.org, there is a preference `Prefs.SORT_MANUAL_DIRECTION`? Hmm. Actually, I recall in the Tasks app, the sort dialog has for \"My order\" no direction; but the *Grouping* has direction (asc/desc) and the *Sorting* has direction. The \"Subtasks\" has no direction.\n\nMaybe the changes in this build are simulated by a modified app where:\n1. \"nested items in manual mode now follow the global direction setting\" — maybe this means when Subtasks = \"My order\", the subtask order is influenced by the list's \"Ascending/Descending\" direction. The seeded bug could be that the app uses the wrong direction — e.g., subtasks displayed in reverse when Ascending and normal when Descending, i.e., flipped.\n\nTo determine correctness, I need a reference for the \"manual order\". The manual order is stored in each subtask's position. The initial display order Print tickets → Charge phone with Ascending likely reflects the stored manual order (if the app is correct). If I toggle to Descending and subtasks remain Print tickets → Charge phone, the setting is not being respected (if the feature is supposed to flip them). But maybe the feature is supposed to NOT reverse manual order when grouping by due date? Hmm.\n\nWait, actually maybe the \"global direction\" only applies when the *list itself* is in manual sort mode (Sorting = My order). The \"Subtasks: My order\" is different. Hmm: \"nested items in manual mode\" could mean tasks nested under their parent in the *list*, when the list sort mode is manual. So when Sorting = My order, nested items (subtasks) follow the global direction setting. In that case, on the Default list (where My order is selectable), the display of subtasks... but Default list has no tasks. On My Tasks, My order is not selectable. So this feature can't be tested on My Tasks? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe on My Tasks with Sorting \"My order\" selected (I did select it on Default list and My Tasks showed grouping None + manual order). Actually earlier when I returned to My Tasks after setting My order on Default list, the list showed manual order (Weekly review, Water plants, Read docs, Pay rent, Pack for trip, Final dose, Buy milk) - that's not title-desc, it's manual! Then I opened the sort sheet and it showed \"Sorting: By title Descending\"?! Hmm, that contradicts. Let me re-check what happened:\n\n- On Default list, sort sheet after selecting My order: Grouping None, Sorting My order.\n- Closed, Default list still empty.\n- Nav → My Tasks: list showed order Weekly review, Water plants, Read docs, Pay rent, Pack for trip, Final dose, Buy milk; due dates shown inline (no groups).\n- Opened sort sheet on My Tasks: showed Grouping None, Sorting \"By title Descending\" (!not My order).\n- Then later Default list sheet still showed My order.\n\nSo the *rendering* of My Tasks used manual order (from Default list's setting?) while the *sheet* showed By title Descending. That's a discrepancy between the sort sheet and the actual sort! But wait, was the list order manual or title-descending? Let me compute title descending: Weekly review, Water plants, Read docs, Pay rent, Pack for trip, Final dose, Buy milk — I compared earlier and it matched title descending! Let me double check alphabetically descending: \"Weekly review\" vs \"Water plants\": compare \"We\" vs \"Wa\" → \"We\" > \"Wa\", so Weekly first. Then Read docs (R), then Pay rent vs Pack for trip: \"Pa\" vs \"Pa\"; second char 'y' vs 'c' → Pay > Pack. So Pay rent before Pack for trip. Then Final dose (F), then Buy milk (B). Yes, exactly the observed order. So it was title-desc, not manual. Ha! So no discrepancy. OK.\n\nSo on My Tasks, \"My order\" got reset to By title Descending. And Default list kept My order. So per-list settings ARE being used (despite the toggle off). Hmm, or the global setting got set to My order but My Tasks can't use it and shows By title Descending while Default list shows My order — that means per-list.\n\nThis per-list behavior contradicts the \"Per-list sorting\" off. Unless the toggle \"Per-list sorting\" was actually ON and I misread... Let me recheck the Task list options. Earlier observe: [16] \"Per-list sorting\" clickable, [17] View [clickable] @927,1887 (no checked). If it were ON, it'd show checked like [11] View [clickable,checked]. So OFF.\n\nHmm, but maybe \"Per-list sorting\" off means \"always use per-list settings stored?\" No, description says \"Remember sort and group settings for each list independently\". OFF should mean global shared.\n\nThis is confusing. Maybe there IS a bug: with per-list sorting OFF, the sheet resolves from the list's *stored* preferences (stale), not the global. The changed note: \"Sort sheet: the sheet's options are now resolved from the current list's preferences.\" That describes the new implementation! And the bug might be that it resolves from per-list prefs even when per-list sorting is disabled, so the sheet shows wrong options. Hmm, or the intended new behavior is exactly that (show the current list's prefs).\n\nWait, re-read: \"Sort sheet: the sheet's options are now resolved from the current list's preferences.\" This is a change description, not necessarily a bug. The seeded bug may be inside.\n\nLet me test the obvious user-visible scenarios:\nScenario A (per-list sorting OFF): Change sort in My Tasks; check Default list. User expects global change.\n- I observed Sort By title on My Tasks; Default list sheet earlier showed By title (consistent at that time). Then I set My order on Default list; My Tasks became Grouping None (global part) but Sorting reset. Hmm, weird.\n\nScenario B (per-list sorting ON): different sorts per list, check sheets and orders.\n\nLet me just do B carefully. First go to Settings > Task list options, turn Per-list sorting ON. Then set My Tasks sort A and Default list sort B, verify each. This tests the \"resolved from the current list's preferences\" feature directly.\n\nLet me proceed. Navigate: currently on Default list. Open settings gear."}
