{"type": "thinking", "text": "Key finding! With Per-list sorting OFF, Default list's sort sheet shows \"Sorting: By due date Descending\" while My Tasks shows \"Sorting: By title Ascending\". If per-list sorting is OFF (settings shared globally), the sheet should show the same options for both lists. The changed item says \"the sheet's options are now resolved from the current list's preferences\" — maybe that's the bug: it resolves from the *list's* preferences even when per-list sorting is off, so it shows stale/different options and the list order is sorted by that stale preference.\n\nBut wait, we need to check the *actual list order* on Default list — it's empty so can't. Hmm, so maybe the list content follows the global but the sheet shows per-list? We can't tell on Default list (empty). Could make a task there temporarily... Actually I could create a probe again to check the order, but that's more data churn.\n\nHold on. Is it truly wrong? The description of the setting: \"Per-list sorting: Remember sort and group settings for each list independently.\" OFF → don't remember per list → use global. So yes, Default list's sheet should show My Tasks' global setting (By title Ascending) when OFF. It shows By due date Descending → inconsistent. Unless with per-list OFF the *last list used* preference is global for each view but not shared... no.\n\nHmm, maybe the app stores sort preferences per list regardless and \"Per-list sorting\" only controls whether *new* lists inherit the global defaults? Hmm. The wording \"Remember sort and group settings for each list independently\" suggests ON = each list independent. OFF = all share. So the observed divergence is likely a bug.\n\nWait, but did the Default list even get its own prefs persisted while per-list was ON? Yes, I set By priority Descending with per-list ON. Then turned OFF. Now Default list shows By due date Descending (not even By priority) — so its per-list pref changed to By due date Descending. Where did that come from? Hmm! Maybe when toggling per-list sorting OFF, all lists got reset to the global default? But My Tasks shows By title Ascending. Hmm, then both should be By title Ascending.\n\nAlternatively, the Default list's sheet is showing something derived from... hmm, \"By due date Descending\" was My Tasks' setting earlier (before I changed to By title). And the Default list's own last setting while per-list ON was By priority Descending. Neither matches. Hmm, maybe the sheet on Default list shows the *global* default from before (By due date Descending) while My Tasks shows its own remembered (By title Ascending)?\n\nConfusing. It's likely a real bug but hard to pin the expected. Let me think about what the \"changed\" feature intends: \"Sort sheet: the sheet's options are now resolved from the current list's preferences.\" This means: previously the sheet showed the *global* options; now it shows the *current list's* options. The bug could be that the sheet now shows the current list's settings but **the task list itself still sorts by the global preferences**, i.e., the sheet lies. Or vice versa.\n\nTo detect, I can create a probe task set in Default list and check its order vs the sheet. But with only 1 task, no order difference. I could create 2 probe tasks in Default list with different titles/dates to see the order. Hmm, data churn twice. Alternatively, move existing tasks? No.\n\nAlternatively, I can add two temporary tasks to Default list, check order per sheet (By due date Descending), then delete both. Let me do that. It's testing; reversible.\n\nPlan:\n- With per-list sorting OFF.\n- Default list sheet says Sorting By due date Descending, Grouping By due date Ascending.\n- Create task A \"AA test\" due date earlier (today+1) and task B \"BB test\" due date later (today+2) in Default list view. With grouping by due date asc, order by due date asc groups (A then B). If sorted descending, B then A (but grouping asc might still group A's date first... hmm, grouping direction asc means group order asc regardless of sort direction? Then both always A then B). Hmm, grouping by due date with only one task per group makes sort direction irrelevant.\n\nBetter: use Sorting \"By title\" while grouping \"None\" in the sheet, so order is visible. Set Default list sheet: Grouping None, Sorting By title Descending. Then create tasks \"Alpha\" and \"Zeta\"; if sorted desc → Zeta then Alpha. Then verify sheet says same. Also set My Tasks sort distinct (By due date Ascending) so we can detect cross-contamination.\n\nBut honestly, is this heading toward a bug report? The possibly seeded bug in sort sheet might be exactly \"sort sheet options resolved from current list's preferences\" being *wrong*: e.g., when per-list sorting OFF, the sheet should show global (the same as My Tasks) but shows stale per-list. Or when ON, it might show wrong.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the earlier observations with per-list sorting OFF (initial state). Initially: My Tasks sheet = By due date Asc Default. I changed Sorting By title Asc → list order changed. Reopened sheet → By title Asc (persisted). Navigated to Default list, its sheet showed By title Desc later (after I toggled direction on My Tasks). Wait, at that time per-list was OFF and Default list sheet showed \"By title Descending\" — same as My Tasks at that moment! Let me recheck: Yes! After I changed My Tasks to By title Descending, I opened Default list sheet and it showed \"Sorting | By title | Descending\" — consistent with global sharing. \n\nThen I selected \"My order\" on Default list → sheet showed Grouping None, Sorting My order. Then My Tasks sheet showed Grouping None, Sorting By title Descending. So Grouping shared, Sorting reset on My Tasks (because My order unsupported). Then Default list sheet showed Grouping None, Sorting My order. So Sorting diverged (Default list kept My order). Hmm, that's because \"My order\" is not available on My Tasks; the app reset My Tasks' sort to By title Descending. If global, then Default list should also show By title Descending. It kept My order → divergence. But maybe the app treats My order as a per-list capability: My Tasks can't use it, so it falls back just for that view; Default list uses the global My order setting. Hmm, that's arguably reasonable.\n\nThen I set My Tasks Sorting to By due date while Grouping None → Default list still My order. Hmm.\n\nNow after per-list ON then OFF, the Default list shows By due date Descending (while My Tasks By title Asc). This is divergence again.\n\nMaybe the app's \"global\" sort is actually the **last setting used** and per-list settings are always stored; the toggle only affects whether *changes* are saved per list. Hard to say. Given ambiguity, I should not report this unless I find a clear inconsistency between the sheet and the list's actual order on the same screen.\n\nKEY test: On DEFAULT list, does the actual list order match the sheet? If yes, no bug from a user's perspective (the sheet is truthful). The \"per-list sorting off\" semantic is a config nuance; the sheet being per-list might be intended by the change note (\"sheet options resolved from current list's preferences\"). Actually! The change note says exactly that the sheet should resolve from the current list's preferences. So showing By due date Desc for Default list IS the intended new behavior. Fine, no bug.\n\nBut we still need to check the sheet matches the list's actual ordering. On My Tasks, sheet By title Asc, list top-level matches title asc. On Default list (empty), no tasks. Let me test with probe tasks in Default list to confirm the list uses the sheet's sort. If it doesn't, that's the bug: the sheet says one thing, list sorts another.\n\nLet me set Default list to something distinctive and create two probe tasks. Actually, we can avoid creating tasks: the sheet says By due date Descending, Grouping By due date Ascending. If I later move an existing task into Default l