{"type": "thinking", "text": "The default sort now shows Water plants, Final dose, Weekly review (manual tie order) — because Sorting is By title Asc? Hmm no, title ascending would be Final dose first. Wait, the \"Due Monday Dec 14\" group shows Water plants, Final dose, Weekly review. That's due-date sort with manual tie-break, not title. Hmm! But I set My Tasks Sorting to By title Ascending and verified the sheet. Did it revert? Let me check: maybe my last action on Default list set Sorting By due date ascending and since per-list sorting is now OFF, it propagated globally to My Tasks (both lists share). Earlier My Tasks showed By title Asc while Default list showed By due date Desc — that was per-list divergence. After I toggled on Default list to Asc, if global, My Tasks would now be By due date Asc. Yes! That's consistent with per-list OFF global sharing (propagating from Default list to My Tasks). But then the divergence before contradicts... ugh.\n\nWait, previously: per-list ON, My Tasks By title Asc, Default list By priority Desc. Then per-list OFF, checked Default list sheet: By due date Desc (huh? not By priority Desc, not My Tasks' By title). Then I toggled Default list direction twice? I toggled once (Desc→Asc). Now My Tasks shows due-date order. Hmm, so maybe when per-list sorting is turned OFF, it picks up the last \"global\" from somewhere (By due date Desc) rather than either list's setting, then changes propagate globally.\n\nIs that a bug? Maybe the \"global\" setting was By due date Desc from earlier (I set My Tasks By due date Desc at one point). Then when per-list ON, My Tasks retained By title Asc; Default list By priority Desc. When OFF, both revert to the global By due date Desc. Then I changed Default list (global) to Asc → My Tasks changes too. That's self-consistent! So per-list sorting OFF uses a saved global setting, and ON uses per-list. Great — no bug there. I was confusing myself. The sheet resolution is correct.\n\nSo the sort sheet works. Fine.\n\nCurrent state: global (per-list OFF) sort = By due date Ascending, Grouping By due date Ascending, Subtasks My order — original! Good.\n\nNow, back to subtask direction question. The \"global direction setting\" is likely the global sort direction (Ascending/Descending) which now applies to subtasks in manual mode. Our test with Sorting Descending didn't flip subtasks... but maybe because Grouping direction? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe \"nested items in manual mode\" refers to nested items when the list's *Sorting is \"My order\"* (manual). In that mode, the global direction setting might be a \"Manual sort direction\" that isn't exposed when My order is selected on My Tasks... Hmm.\n\nActually! Maybe the global direction setting IS the \"Grouping Ascending/Descending\" direction of the sort sheet. Wait no.\n\nHmm, let me look at the app's \"sort direction\" for **grouping**: The Grouping row has direction Ascending/Descending. When grouping By due date, direction affects order of groups. In manual mode (grouping None), maybe the global direction \"Grouping Ascending\" is used for nested manual items. Let me test toggling Grouping direction to Descending and see if subtask order flips. Currently Grouping Asc. Let's try. If subtask order flips with Grouping direction, then that's the \"global direction setting\"! And maybe the bug: it follows Grouping direction even though Sorting direction is Asc? Hmm, the expected is unclear.\n\nLet me test quickly: set Grouping Descending, Subtasks My order, check subtasks."}
