{"type": "thinking", "text": "Subtasks By title Desc did flip. So the direction toggle works for subtask sorting.\n\nNow set Subtasks back to \"My order\" and observe the order and whether a direction toggle appears (it disappears). In My order mode, what direction does it use? Observed earlier: Print tickets, Charge phone (reverse of editor's manual order Charge phone, Print tickets). Since the subtask direction was NOT visible in My order mode, maybe it inherits the last direction (Descending now!). If the app now shows Print tickets, Charge phone (descending), then it \"follows the global direction setting\" — where the global direction is the Subtasks direction (last value Descending). Then if I set the Subtasks direction to Ascending before switching to My order, it should show Charge phone, Print tickets. Since the direction toggle disappears after choosing My order, the \"global direction\" might be the previous direction value.\n\nWait, when I first observed (initial state), Subtasks \"My order\" with no direction. The stored subtask sort direction was maybe ascending. And display Print tickets first = descending-ish. Hmm, if ascending direction stored, the expected is Charge phone first. It showed Print tickets first. So bug.\n\nLet me test: set Subtasks By title Ascending (which shows Charge phone then Print tickets), then switch Subtasks to My order. If the display becomes Charge phone, Print tickets, then manual mode follows the direction (ascending) correctly. If it jumps to Print tickets, Charge phone, then manual mode ignores direction / always reversed.\n\nDo it: Subtasks By title Ascending → check order C,P → then Subtasks My order → check order."}
