{"type": "thinking", "text": "Nested order still Print tickets then Charge phone with \"New tasks on top\" OFF. So not that either.\n\nHmm wait, the list scrolled to top. Nested order is still P then C.\n\nLet me check the sort sheet shows Subtasks My order still. Yes presumably.\n\nOK so nested manual order is simply P, C regardless of any direction. The editor shows C, P. So there's a real inconsistency between the editor and the list. Which is the bug? The changed area mentions the task list. According to the change, nested items in manual mode should follow the global direction setting. Since nothing changes the list order, I'd report: \"the nested subtask order in My order mode doesn't follow the global direction; Ascending vs Descending produces the same order (Print tickets before Charge phone).\"\n\nHmm, hold on. Let me reconsider what \"global direction setting\" might refer to. Maybe there's a *sort direction* preference exposed in the **per-list settings** when \"Per-list sorting\" is ON? Hmm no.\n\nCould \"global direction\" mean the **device's layout direction** (LTR/RTL)? Honestly, \"global direction setting\" is an odd phrase for sort direction. Usually you'd say \"sort direction\". \"Global direction setting\" sounds like a global setting that controls \"direction\" — maybe the \"New tasks on top\" (direction of adding). Hmm.\n\nHmm, maybe it's the **\"Manual\" sort direction** in the app's general settings, which I haven't found. Let me search the Android app's settings screens thoroughly with the search? There's no settings search.\n\nAnother idea: Maybe the \"global direction setting\" is in the **grouping** row's direction when **Grouping = None**... no.\n\nWait, actually! I remember: Tasks.org has a setting **\"Sort direction\"** for **\"New tasks\"**? Hmm no.\n\nLet me look at the app's version/settings via About? no.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the changed feature refers to the **\"Subtask nesting\"** in the task list when **\"Subtasks\" sort = My order**, and the \"global direction setting\" is the **reverse order toggle in the settings for the list** accessible via **long-press on the sort button**? Hmm.\n\nLet me long-press the Sort button — maybe it opens settings or reveals direction options. Might be worth trying."}
